    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nThank you for the great project. According to the documentation, Nerd Fonts is an option for statusline. However, the current default behavior requires Nerd Fonts and moreover, it is a bit hard to disable Nerd Fonts. Hence, we add the new option 'nerdfonts' to disable easily. Cheers,",
    "closed_at": "2022-06-14T07:02:12Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi! Thanks for contribution, it looks relevant.\r\n\r\nIs there a reason of why not use `Git` and `LSP` as custom icons in `args`? Like `MiniStatusline.section_git({ trunc_width = 75, icon = 'Git' })`. I understand that this will need custom active content function (possibly quite verbose), but anything else besides this?\r\n\r\nI am more curious about `MiniStatusline.section_fileinfo()` with `nvim-web-devicons` installed. Does it work incorrectly without Nerd font (shows weird square in place of an actual icon)?",
