        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Is there a reason of why not use Git and LSP as custom icons in args? Like MiniStatusline.section_git({ trunc_width = 75, icon = 'Git' }). I understand that this will need custom active content function (possibly quite verbose), but anything else besides this?\r\n\r\nTrue. This is the reason why I created it. Currently, I am using `MiniStatusline.section_git` to suppress NerdFonts. Let me introduce my problem more.\r\n\r\nMiniStatusline has  fantastic optional parameters to decorate statusline.\r\n\r\n- `git` status: it will be disabled if `gitsign. nvim` is disabled.\r\n- `fileinfo` status: it will fall back if `kyazdani42/nvim-web-devicons` is disabled.\r\n\r\nThe above option provides the fallback-mechanism if they are disabled.\r\nHowever, the NerdFonts has no fallback-mechanism, that is, we need to manually make\r\nstatusline function to fallback. This is harder than others. Of course, I know that font detection is impossible from the terminal version of Neovim. Instead, I propose an easier way to disable it manually to fill the gap. \r\n\r\nFurther, we do not change any lines about section_fileinfo. Thus, it should work well.",
