        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for explanation. I understand your reasoning more clear now.\r\n\r\n> Further, we do not change any lines about section_fileinfo. Thus, it should work well.\r\n\r\nI understand that. What I tried to ask you (as at the moment I can't reproduce \"non-nerd-font\" environment), is how it works *right now* under following conditions:\r\n- Non-nerd-font.\r\n- 'nvim-web-devicons' installed.\r\n- `section_fileinfo()` active.\r\n\r\nI imagine, it should act similarly to icons in git and diagnostic sections, but not sure.\r\n\r\nAll in all, at the moment I am more inclined to add this option, but in more general `use_icons` form. If `false`:\r\n- In `section_git()` fallback to `\"Git\"` (as you implemented).\r\n- In `section_diagnostic()` fallback to some short string indicating diagnostic. `\"LSP\"` is fine, but something more targeted would be better.\r\n- In `section_fileinfo()` fallback to as if 'nvim-web-devicons' is not installed.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it a little bit more and get back to you, hopefully, tomorrow.",
